Action: GetResources
Action Input: {"resource_type": "pods", "namespace": "boutique", "output_wide": true}

Thought: All pods are Running, so the disruption is likely service-level configuration or connectivity rather than pod crash. Next, inspect Service definitions and endpoints for selector/port anomalies.
Action: GetResources
Action Input: {"resource_type": "services", "namespace": "boutique", "output_wide": true}

Thought: The pods list has no emailservice pod, while its Service exists; all other pods are Running. This points to a deployment/replica or scheduling fault for emailservice. I’ll inspect deployment status to confirm.
Action: GetResources
Action Input: {"resource_type":"deployments","namespace":"boutique","output_wide":true}

Thought: Emailservice is the only workload unavailable, and its Deployment shows desired 1 but zero up-to-date replicas, with no emailservice Pod present. I need the Deployment conditions/events to determine why no replica was created.
Action: DescribeResource
Action Input: {"resource_type":"deployment","name":"emailservice","namespace":"boutique"}

Thought: The Deployment's ReplicaSet failed to create any Pod (`FailedCreate`). Describing the ReplicaSet should reveal the exact creation error, such as quota, admission, or service account failure.
Action: DescribeResource
Action Input: {"resource_type": "replicaset", "name": "emailservice-6d4d7cd4dc", "namespace": "boutique"}

